l claim that takes on unearned strength"}],"text":"A lab keeps dummy blood bags for training, and when a real patient test is needed a technician tests a dummy bag instead of the patient's available sample and reports the result as the patient's reading."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A readiness claim rests on a synthetic corpus fixture and is reported as real coverage, although the actual public-safe corpus was available.","does_not_prove":"Using real material leaves open whether that material is correct or complete, and declared synthetic fixtures remain allowed.","enforced_in_component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol","corpus_readiness_mathlib_absence_gate"],"example":{"component_ids":["macro_projection_import_protocol"],"text":"The source-import protocol brings in real public-safe material by manifest and content hash, so a real claim rests on real input that can be traced by its hash."},"governs":"Whether a claim rests on a real input or a made-up one.","plain":"The mistake of building a real conclusion on a made-up input when genuine, shareable material was available, so the made-up input gives the conclusion strength it never earned.","potential_misread":"That a stand-in can carry the same weight as the real input because it looks the same on the page.","refuses":"Using a synthetic fixture in place of available public-safe material and letting the claim take on strength real inputs never gave it.","requires":"Real public-safe material behind any claim others rely on, or, when only a fixture is available, an input labelled synthetic and a claim given no weight.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"Readers can tell whether a result rests on something real and shareable or on a convenient placeholder, and decide how much to rely on it."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"ANTI_PRINCIPLES.md::AP-12","statement":"| ID | Violated axioms | Rejected failure shape |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AP-12 Synthetic substrat